COMMAND|H=<blobless full-history clone of USIM>|W=<new empty directory>|steps=export GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1; mkdir -p $W/in $W/script; dd if=gguf/universe-simulator/gguf/ASOLARIA-CONSTELLATION.gguf of=$W/in/FABLE5-SELF-SEED-3078.hbi bs=1 skip=93216 count=3078 status=none; python3 -I gguf/codex/tools/stage_office.py --commit 37248b2 --names-from 7ca9ce5 --hist $H --laws-dir docs/handoffs/acer-post60d-2026-10-18/FABLE5-REGEN-ITEM4-QR-CODEXES-AND-HRM-2026-10-18/qr-codexes --prior qr/colour-qr/vendor/universe-simulator/key/prior3174.bin --remove FABLE5-ABSORB-ALL-MATRICES.hbp --replace FABLE5-SELF-SEED-3078.hbi=$W/in/FABLE5-SELF-SEED-3078.hbi --wasm 4ea2ae3:web/asolaria_tribit.wasm --no-constellation --dest $W/stage; cp docs/handoffs/acer-post60d-2026-10-18/FABLE5-REGEN-ITEM4-QR-CODEXES-AND-HRM-2026-10-18/qr-readers/constellation/project_gguf.py $W/script/; cd $W/stage && python3 -I ../script/project_gguf.py|tools=gguf/codex/tools/stage_office.py sha256 ba3d26a990ad2641549d0d255497166ca38a5cac42ae608c197c948dceb9dce3 (commit 539d745)|python=python3 -I, 3.13.16, standard library only|json=0
CAVEAT|text=15878 B of the target's inputs were public only inside the target itself (the 4 qr files 12800 B and FABLE5-SELF-SEED-3078.hbi 5c040e04 3078 B; CODEX-REGENERATE.md:380). In this run the qr files come from ACER's delivery, but FABLE5-SELF-SEED-3078.hbi is still cut from the target. project_gguf.py:163-170 copies each input unchanged into its own I8 tensor. A match therefore proves that the projection is deterministic over these inputs. It does not prove that the target can be rebuilt from bytes outside the target|json=0
